Package: SegStability
Type: Package
Title: Descriptive Segmentation Sensitivity in Spatial Transcriptomics
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: person("Rama Krishna", "Pudota",
    email = "ramakrishnapudota36@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0009-2804-8915"))
Description: Quantifies correspondence between alternative cell segmentations
    of the same molecule-resolved spatial transcriptomics experiment. Preserves
    an immutable molecule universe, exact molecule identities, complete cell
    censuses, and explicit assignment statuses when constructing weighted
    shared-molecule graphs. Describes categorical cell-state stability,
    directional support sensitivity, optional spatial topology and polygon
    overlap, and agreement among stochastic segmentation runs. Results describe
    sensitivity to segmentation choices and do not estimate segmentation
    accuracy or establish biological ground truth.
